      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel that nothing is worth saving when the foundation feels gone. The idea of \"reclaiming\" something when everything feels ash is an impossible burden to place on yourself right now. Sometimes, the only true act of self-care is allowing the exhaustion to simply *be*, without the pressure to perform or pretend. You don't have to rebuild; you can just let the quiet settle for a while.",
      "source": "target",
